es/106444","id":2910742665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tfmiJ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T23:08:28Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T23:10:12Z","body":"I wonder if we should have some kind of default value to encourage the use of a standard prefix. Is there any established prefix out there?\r\n\r\nUsing `$$` isn't too bad as a default (it's very unlikely to be used in existing projects for localizable strings). A single `$` is more prone to false positives though (e.g. the text `$100 bill` might be localizable in a project as an item name).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910742665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910743947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106444#issuecomment-2910743947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106444","id":2910743947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tfm2L","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T23:09:32Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T23:10:46Z","body":"I'm open to changing the default, I use `$` in my project.\r\nI'm not sure if there is any standard, this might be a Godot-only problem 😅","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910743947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943456183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106444#issuecomment-2943456183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106444","id":2943456183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vcZO3","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T09:34:33Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T09:34:33Z","body":"I'm not convinced by the use case yet. I could see why one could want some strings to not be extracted, but I'd assume it to be strings that one wants to keep unmodified in the game. But here the prefix would make these strings unsuitable for in-game use, unless manually edited from code, at which point handling the translations manually is as easy.\r\n\r\nYour use case seems to be specifically about some placeholder strings only visible in the editor that get replaced at runtime. How many strings do you have that fit this pattern? This seems like a pretty niche use case and I doubt many would have similar needs, or discover that there's a feature that supports this pattern.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943456183/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943555874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106444#issuecomment-2943555874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106444","id":2943555874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vcxki","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T10:05:08Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T10:05:08Z","body":"> How many strings do you have that fit this pattern?\r\n\r\n37\r\n\r\n> But here the prefix would make these strings unsuitable for in-game use, unless manually edited from code, at which point handling the translations manually is as easy.\r\n\r\nIt's getting more complicated, because I'd have to move the code to `NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED`. I didn't check how easy would that be, but I doubt it would be simple everywhere.\r\n\r\n___\r\n\r\ntbh I'd be fine if we had an easier way to customize strings in POT generator. Something like `_process_strings(strings: PackedStringArray)`, where you can add and remove from the array. I could manually filter out prefixed stuff. I need to add strings too, and this PR does not cover that.\r\n\r\nI'm doing it anyway now, but I have to manually parse and rewrite the POT file :/","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943555874/reactions","total_cou